Let $A_1,\dots,A_m\subseteq[n]$ have sizes divisible by $3$, while no $|A_i\cap A_j|$, $i\ne j$, is divisible by $3$. Show that $m\le1+n+\binom n2$.
\end{exercise} Exact domains and endpoint checks: Supplied p3,L1/2 substitution is correct. Independent direct degree-two polynomials(v dot x-1)(v dot x-2) have diagonal2, off-diagonal0; multilinear feature count1+n+binom n2. n0/1 and automatic distinctness included.

