\begin{exercise}[$\star$]\label{combinatorial:ex:cdsharp}
Show that equality holds in the Cauchy--Davenport theorem when $A$ and $B$ are arithmetic progressions with the same difference and $|A|+|B|\le p+1$. Show that the theorem fails in $\Z/4\Z$.
\end{exercise} Exact domains and endpoint checks: Supplied interval-sum argument matches first derivation; nonzero difference gives no repeats beforep. Independently translate/dilate and enumerate all small lengths including full-field boundary k+l=p+1 and singleton. Z4 subgroup counterexample exact.

