Show that a cap set in $\mathbb F_3^2$ has at most $4$ points.
\end{exercise} Exact domains and endpoint checks: First parallel-class pair count(10 pairs vs8) and affine-normalization method are both independent of supplied answer. Actual answer gives third method: each line through a cap point contains another; lines through an outside point force an even total, contradict5. Every five-subset of nine points and the four-corner cap checked.

